{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1505787-when-and-how-to-handle-the-realm-civil-war-in-a-secondary-school-game","id":1505787,"title":"When and how to handle the Realm Civil War in a Secondary School Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-19T09:56:58-07:00","id":1505787,"title":"When and how to handle the Realm Civil War in a Secondary School Game","content":"I'm plotting out a DB secondary school game, and I'm wondering where and how to have the Realm Civil War impact the place.<br /> <br /> Secondary schools are attended from the ages of 15 to 21, a span of six years. The present day is RY 768, five years after the Empress vanishes, four years after the Council of the Empty Throne, and three years after Tepet's fall and the splitting of the Imperial Legions. Most importantly, it also leaves three years before the formal &quot;abdication&quot; of the Empress, which is where I imagine the civil war would kick off properly.<br /> <br /> Given these timescales, I'm curious about when would be the more interesting times for a secondary school game, without disintegrating it as a low-stakes game. I'd imagine that a civil war would have severe implications for any structured education in the Realm, which means that feasibly any high school game that wants to avoid the Civil War entirely would have to start before the disappearance of the Empress.<br /> <br /> Has anyone run games that go through the whole length of a secondary school education, and how did you handle the various big events for the Realm alongside the more immediate things happening in the school? I imagine any Tepet PC would have letters from somewhere telling of the Battle of Futile Blood, and handling their grief from the death of family members as a matter of course, but how else have these events been managed? Or do folks tend to just run these games in the time before the Empress disappears, avoiding it entirely? I imagine that'll at the very least impact how House Tepet is seen, and House V'neef is even greener than usual.<br /> <br /> This is a bit rambly, but I'm just curious how people have dealt with the macro Realm calendar in a secondary school game context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T01:01:12-07:00","id":1512097,"title":"","content":"A couple fo thoughts from someone who is starting their own secondary school game set in the civil war: It really depends on how much you want the civil war plot to be part of your game. It is entirely possible that it is happening in the background and may provide motivations for some instructors/students but never intrude directly. OR at the other end of the s[ectrum one faction or another ocupies the school and treats the kids as hostages / a resources to develop. <br /> <br /> As far as timing goes: at the end of the Regent's term the throne will officially be declared vacant. Mnemon has already announced her intent to take the throne at that point, more or less daring anyone to stop her. Waiting until the go-date is the privelige of the front-runner, many who are less sure of their ability to claim the throne may want to gain an advantage with a pre-emptive strike before then. After all if they are triggering a civil war then violating that one edict won't really matter much. If they win then ti doesn't matter and if they lose well, it is unlikely that the winners wouldn't retaliate against them regardless of the date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T02:44:18-07:00","id":1514673,"title":"","content":"Which school?<br /> <br /> In my game, the Heptagram raised every magical defense it had, declared neutrality and waited for someone to win. (The PCs had long graduated before the civil war began, but still had ties to the school.)<br /> <br /> You could play being trapped on a magical island as war unfolds around you.<br /> <br /> Having relatively young Dynasts (first years) would be perfect for such a game.<br /> <br /> By contrast the Spiral Academy is literally in the capital city. It will come under siege. If you have, for example, Ragara students and Mnemon takes the capital, you can expect a polite knock from Mnemon legions on your character's bedroom door.<br /> <br /> Having relatively old students (final years) would make a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> And this also affects timings.<br /> <br /> If you are going for a Spiral Academy game, then kicking off the Realm Civil War early makes sense: your parents knew that conflict was brewing, but still sent you to the capital because the Council of the Vacant Throne suggested you still had a year or two of safety under the Regent before hostilities started. Whereas with the Heptagram idea, maybe your parents sent you to the Isle of Voices specifically to get you out of the way of the civil war.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah, just don't start your game in RY768. Go earlier and sidestep the issue entirely. Or Deus Ex it and have the Deliberative vote for five more years of Tepet Fokuf.<br /> <br /> I think it might be interesting to run the game at Pasiap's Stair. Be Outcastes learning about Dynastic society. Then civil war. You are military trained but don't have an allegiance to any particular house. How do you navigate this? What do the Great Houses think about having a super solider school on their doorstep when the soldiers don't owe them any particular loyalty? You can do politicking for alliance. Defending the school from attacks. Go mercenary or full bandit. Throw in with a Great House. Declare your alliance to the Scarlet Empress and go Wyld Hunting whilst the Realm disintegrates around you. Maybe even side with The People and lead your own glorious revolution against the status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T12:11:37-07:00","id":1515548,"title":"","content":"A lot of what might happen is dependant on your vision of how the overall Civil War will go. To what level will the intrigues rise? How bad will the actual violence be? Will it remain somewhat under the surface, or will it be an actual war, where all pretenses are shed and armies are marching, while all House members are extected to actively participate? Notice, that once a danger level rises beyond certain point (probably even before reaching the outright war stage), everyone will just start pulling their scions home, to safety - or towards the frontlines. And that means not just students, but teachers as well.<br /> So, at first you will see tensions rising, and preexisting personal relations affected by current House politics. Then you will see groups of students band into alliances for safety more and more, as well as teachers playing favouritism (and acting against each other) in more and more visible ways. Then people will start to disappear. Some by getting recalled, some by fleeing (especially from more minor families)... and some in more final way. At some point everything will just unravel, or one House will march in and take over.<br /> Each of the schools will likely be affected in different ways and at different rates, but ultimately all will get affected, due to Dynast staff in those generally not being able to avoid the whole issue (and mortal teachers being unable to keep everything running on their own).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T15:45:38-07:00","id":1524155,"title":"","content":"One element could be students given an accelerated curriculum and early graduating early, if the realm is still in a &quot;cold&quot; civil war but the anathema start becoming a bigger problem. Issues could arise as the school is &quot;hollowed out&quot; with less and less senior students. <br /> <br /> One area you could potentially look for, are novels set in college or high school during the American civil war to mine for material. I'm aware this is a highly obscure sub-sub-sub genre but some might exist, especially as romance novels, which is renown for a plethora of sub genres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T15:44:46-07:00","id":1524441,"title":"","content":"I would probably start it before the civil war begins<br /> With the Houses trying to pressure the new exalts to undermine their classmates ahead of the real fighting<br /> Once the civil war actually starts, this would move to the Houses trying to call their children home to fight<br /> Do the young exalts answer their families calls or do they disobey and do their own thing?<br /> If they choose to disobey then you can get into whether the school offers them sanctuary or if they have to flee the realm or fight a insurgent battle across the realm<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28208-broken-golden-lion","name":"Broken Golden Lion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T15:41:35-08:00","id":1526086,"title":"","content":"This is probably only tangentially relevant (if at all), but maybe it will serve someone as inspiration. A few years ago, I read Pat Conroy's <i>The Lords of Discipline</i>, a novel about attending (a fictional version of) the Citadel military academy during the Vietnam War. I remember a few details of how the war created an ever-present undercurrent of both dread and patriotic jingoism amongst the students. As a military academy during wartime, the students were (almost) all expected to have a career as officers in the military right after graduation. Of course, many of the graduates were sent off to Vietnam and were killed while newer students arrived at the academy. The academy began a tradition of hanging the killed graduates' portraits on the walls of the lower floor of the school library, which was fine in the beginning of the war. But as more and more smiling pictures of dead boys began covering up almost all of the walls of the library's first floor, students began avoiding the first floor entirely as they didn't want to be distracted by the portraits while they were trying to study. The students even took to nicknaming the library's first floor as &quot;the body bag.&quot; It was also mentioned that the school consulted an architect about expanding the library to have room for portraits of all the war's projected casualties. The architect promptly said that a <i>whole new building </i>would need to be built for all those additional portraits.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what it would look like in-universe if something like this was tried at the Realm's academies after the Civil War began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T15:50:03-08:00","id":1526087,"title":"","content":"A monolith with engraved names would probably be more likely. Portraits are expensive, and the Immaculates tend to be aniconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T08:54:42-08:00","id":1526679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1505787-when-and-how-to-handle-the-realm-civil-war-in-a-secondary-school-game?p=1526086#post1526086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably only tangentially relevant (if at all), but maybe it will serve someone as inspiration. A few years ago, I read Pat Conroy's <i>The Lords of Discipline</i>, a novel about attending (a fictional version of) the Citadel military academy during the Vietnam War. I remember a few details of how the war created an ever-present undercurrent of both dread and patriotic jingoism amongst the students. As a military academy during wartime, the students were (almost) all expected to have a career as officers in the military right after graduation. Of course, many of the graduates were sent off to Vietnam and were killed while newer students arrived at the academy. The academy began a tradition of hanging the killed graduates' portraits on the walls of the lower floor of the school library, which was fine in the beginning of the war. But as more and more smiling pictures of dead boys began covering up almost all of the walls of the library's first floor, students began avoiding the first floor entirely as they didn't want to be distracted by the portraits while they were trying to study. The students even took to nicknaming the library's first floor as &quot;the body bag.&quot; It was also mentioned that the school consulted an architect about expanding the library to have room for portraits of all the war's projected casualties. The architect promptly said that a <i>whole new building </i>would need to be built for all those additional portraits.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what it would look like in-universe if something like this was tried at the Realm's academies after the Civil War began.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would not translate well into the Realm Civil War situation. You can't make an attempt at unification and generating patriotism when the fight is internal, and the conflict lines exist within the institution itself. If anything, something like that would drive the wedge even further, inciting even greater animosity among the students.<br /> <br /> Think what would have happened if that &quot;military academy&quot; was a school not just for Americans, but also for French, Chinese, Russians, and Vietnamese (from <i>both</i> Vietcong and South Vietnam groups). It would not be pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T16:03:54-07:00","id":1535871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1505787-when-and-how-to-handle-the-realm-civil-war-in-a-secondary-school-game?p=1526679#post1526679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would not translate well into the Realm Civil War situation. You can't make an attempt at unification and generating patriotism when the fight is internal, and the conflict lines exist within the institution itself. If anything, something like that would drive the wedge even further, inciting even greater animosity among the students.<br /> <br /> Think what would have happened if that &quot;military academy&quot; was a school not just for Americans, but also for French, Chinese, Russians, and Vietnamese (from <i>both</i> Vietcong and South Vietnam groups). It would not be pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Going into something of a tangent but decidedly related, what about the massive <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protests_of_1968\" target=\"_blank\">worldwide wave</a> of anti-war student protests that occured in the period?<br /> <br /> A lot of countries had their own particular brand of anti-establishment youth resistance and that could make for an interesting monkeywrench, specially if elements of the Immaculate Order or disgruntled outcastes all across the Isle decide to throw in their support.<br /> <br /> Damn, i can definitely see House Ledaal getting tempted to support considering how many in their own leadership would much prefer to be battling outside/existential threats instead of all this petty infighting circling the empty throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}